      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality**: Correctly restores the `EC_CMD_GET_PROTOCOL_INFO` host command handler (`spi_get_protocol_info`) on non-FPMCU STM32 boards with `CONFIG_SPI` enabled (`kukui` family, `elm`, `nucleo-f412zg`, `nucleo-h743zi`), while preserving runtime `TRANSPORT_SEL` detection (`UART` vs `SPI`) on `CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU` boards.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: Fits the existing `chip/stm32` build and host command dispatch model (`$(or $(CONFIG_FINGERPRINT_MCU),$(CONFIG_SPI))` in `chip/stm32/build.mk` alongside `#ifndef CONFIG_I2C_PERIPHERAL` in `chip/stm32/host_command_common.c`).\n* **Code Simplicity**: Minor optional suggestion on `chip/stm32/host_command_common.c` to use early returns and deduplicate the `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPI)` / `spi_get_protocol_info(args)` path.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: Consistent with ChromiumOS EC C conventions (`IS_ENABLED(...)` compile-time config checks and kernel-style formatting).\n* **Security**: No security or memory-safety concerns identified.\n* **Testing**: Verified via board builds across affected STM32 targets and on-device protocol v3 verification (`ectool protoinfo`) on `kakadu`.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: Focused, single-purpose cherry-pick (`+16, -13`).\n* **Commit Message**: Clear and thorough explanation of the regression history, impact on kernel protocol v3/v2 probing, and fix. [[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/79b97f82-80df-4199-9b51-c2b7b91d1261)] [🔗](http://go/tj/79b97f82-80df-4199-9b51-c2b7b91d1261)",
